/// Static Markdown documentation of the shop backend's public API.
/// This mixin reads no actor state, so it takes no parameters and declares
/// only `getApiDoc`.
mixin () {
  /// Return the API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    let doc = "# Prateep Commerce — Backend API\n\nA single-shop invoicing and debt-tracking backend for one manager and many\ncustomer accounts. The manager maintains customers, products, invoices,\npayments, and shop settings; customers sign in to view their own invoices,\ndebts, payments, and receipts, and to upload bank-transfer proofs for the\nmanager to approve or reject.\n\nAll money is stored as **satang** (`Nat`), where `100 satang = 1 THB`. The\nfrontend formats satang as THB for display. All timestamps are **Int\nnanoseconds** since the Unix epoch (`mo:core/Time.now()`); the frontend\nconverts them for display.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nThe backend uses Internet Identity. A caller is identified by the principal\nderived from their Internet Identity delegation.\n\n- **Anonymous callers** are treated as `#guest`. Every manager-guarded and\n  customer-guarded endpoint rejects them.\n- **Signed-in callers** must be registered before any role-guarded call\n  succeeds. Registration happens when a caller signs in through the app's own\n  frontend, which calls `_internet_identity_sign_in_finish` (or\n  `_initialize_access_control`) once. The **first** principal to register\n  becomes `#admin` (the manager); every later principal becomes `#user`.\n- A direct API caller that has never signed in through the frontend is\n  **unregistered**, even if it is the app owner. Calling a guarded endpoint\n  while unregistered traps with `User is not registered` (from\n  `getUserRole`). To register directly, call `_initialize_access_control` once\n  as a signed-in caller before any role-guarded call — including guarded\n  queries. The first caller to do so receives `#admin`; subsequent callers\n  receive `#user`.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity **derivation origin**, published\n  at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already\n  holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app\n  principal against that origin (for example\n  `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). A principal derived against a\n  different origin is a **different principal** than the one the frontend\n  registered, so it will be unregistered here. Such a delegation acts with the\n  user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n### Roles\n\n- `#admin` — the manager. Required by every manager endpoint.\n- `#user` — a registered signed-in caller. Customer endpoints additionally\n  require that the caller's principal is linked to a customer account.\n- `#guest` — anonymous.\n\n### Authorization model\n\n- **Manager endpoints** are guarded by `AccessControl.isAdmin`. A non-admin\n  caller traps with `Unauthorized: Only the manager can perform this action`.\n- **Customer endpoints** derive the customer from the caller principal via\n  `customerForPrincipal`; they never accept a client-supplied customer id. A\n  signed-in caller with no linked customer account traps with\n  `Unauthorized: No customer account is linked to this caller`.\n- Customer accounts are created by the manager. `createCustomer` provisions the\n  account with `loginPrincipal = null`. The manager binds a login principal\n  with `bindCustomerLogin(id, principal)` (manager-only), which clears any\n  prior binding on that principal so a principal maps to at most one customer.\n  A signed-in caller may also self-bind to an unclaimed account with\n  `claimCustomerAccount(id)`, which returns `null` when the account already has\n  a login principal.\n- Document endpoints (`getInvoiceDocument`, `getReceiptDocument`,\n  `getDebtNoticeDocument`) allow the manager full access and otherwise require\n  the caller to own the requested document; a mismatch traps with\n  `Unauthorized: This invoice does not belong to you` (or the receipt / debt\n  notice equivalent).\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `Satang` — `Nat`, 100 satang = 1 THB.\n- `Timestamp` — `Int`, nanoseconds since the Unix epoch.\n- Identifiers (`CustomerId`, `ProductId`, `InvoiceId`, `PaymentId`, `ProofId`,\n  `ReceiptId`, `NotificationId`) — `Nat`, assigned sequentially by the backend.\n- `InvoiceStatus` — `#unpaid | #partiallyPaid | #paid | #overdue`.\n- `PaymentStatus` / `ProofStatus` — `#pending | #approved | #rejected`.\n- `PaymentMethod` — `#cash | #bankTransfer | #other`.\n- `AgingBucket` — `#current | #days1to30 | #days31to60 | #days61to90 | #over90`.\n- `NotificationKind` — `#proofUploaded | #invoiceOverdue | #paymentRecorded |\n  #proofApproved | #proofRejected`.\n- `TransferProof.imageKey` — `Text`, the platform file-storage key for the\n  uploaded proof image. The image bytes are not stored in the canister.\n- Optional fields (`?T`) are Candid `opt`; absent means \"unset\".\n\n### Derived values\n\n- **Invoice status is derived**, not stored independently: `#paid` when\n  `amountPaid >= total`; otherwise `#overdue` when `dueAt < now`; otherwise\n  `#partiallyPaid` when `amountPaid > 0`; otherwise `#unpaid`. It is recomputed\n  whenever a payment is recorded or a proof is approved.\n- **`outstanding`** is `total - amountPaid`, floored at 0.\n- **Aging buckets** classify each unpaid invoice by how long it has been due:\n  `#current` when `dueAt >= now`; otherwise by whole days past due —\n  `#days1to30`, `#days31to60`, `#days61to90`, `#over90`.\n- **`amountInWords`** in document responses is the Thai baht text of the amount.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- **Proof review.** `uploadProof` creates a proof with status `#pending` and\n  notifies the manager. `approveProof` creates an approved `#bankTransfer`\n  payment, issues a receipt, recalculates the invoice balance, and notifies the\n  customer. `rejectProof` sets status `#rejected`, records the review note, and\n  **leaves the invoice balance unchanged**.\n- **Payment recording.** `recordPayment` records an approved payment, issues a\n  receipt, recalculates the invoice balance, and notifies the manager.\n- **Notifications.** Manager and customer notifications are append-only rows\n  with a `read` flag. `countUnread*` endpoints are cheap polling targets;\n  `list*` endpoints return newest-first and accept an optional `limit`.\n- **Polling guidance.** Poll `countUnreadManagerNotifications` /\n  `countUnreadMyNotifications` for badge counts, and re-fetch the relevant list\n  when the count changes. All read endpoints are `query` calls and are safe to\n  poll frequently.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- **Idempotent-by-guard.** `approveProof` and `rejectProof` are safe to retry:\n  if the proof is no longer `#pending`, they return the current proof unchanged\n  and create no additional payment, receipt, or notification.\n- **Non-idempotent.** `createCustomer`, `createProduct`, `createInvoice`,\n  `recordPayment`, and `uploadProof` allocate a new sequential id and append a\n  new row on every successful call. Retrying after a timeout can create a\n  duplicate record; check the returned id before retrying.\n- **Idempotent.** `updateCustomer`, `updateProduct`, `deactivateProduct`,\n  `updateSettings`, and the `mark*Read` endpoints overwrite state with the\n  supplied values, so repeating them converges to the same result.\n- **Destructive effects.** `deactivateProduct` sets `active = false` but keeps\n  the product and its invoice history. No endpoint deletes rows.\n- **Notifications are append-only.** Repeating a mutation that pushes a\n  notification appends another notification.\n\n## Errors, traps, and limits\n\n- Authorization failures and unregistered callers **trap** (they do not return\n  an error variant). The trap messages are:\n  - `User is not registered` — signed-in but never registered.\n  - `Unauthorized: Only the manager can perform this action` — non-admin on a\n    manager endpoint.\n  - `Unauthorized: No customer account is linked to this caller` — signed-in\n    caller with no linked customer account.\n  - `Unauthorized: This invoice does not belong to you` (and the receipt / debt\n    notice equivalents) — document ownership mismatch.\n- Lookup endpoints return `null` (Candid `opt`) when the record does not exist\n  rather than trapping.\n- `createInvoice` silently skips line items whose `productId` does not exist;\n  the invoice total is the sum of the resolvable lines only.\n- `recordPayment` accepts an `invoiceId` that does not exist; the resulting row\n  carries empty invoice number / customer fields. `uploadProof` instead traps\n  with `Invoice not found` for an unknown invoice, and with\n  `Unauthorized: This invoice does not belong to the caller` when the invoice\n  belongs to a different customer.\n- `listInvoices` date filters compare against `issuedAt` inclusively.\n- Customer list search matches name and phone; product search matches name and\n  SKU; invoice and payment search match number / customer name / reference.\n  Search is case-insensitive.\n- `listCustomers` `sortBy` accepts `\"name\"` (default), `\"phone\"`,\n  `\"outstanding\"`, or `\"createdAt\"`; `descending` defaults to `false`.\n\n## Manager endpoints\n\n### Customers\n- `listCustomers(filter)` — list customers with derived outstanding balance and\n  invoice count. `filter` = `{ search : ?Text; sortBy : ?Text; descending : ?Bool }`.\n- `getCustomer(id)` — customer detail with outstanding balance, aging, invoice\n  count, and payment count.\n- `createCustomer(input)` — create a customer account. `input` =\n  `{ name; phone; address; creditLimit; notes }`.\n- `updateCustomer(id, input)` — edit a customer account. `input` adds `active`.\n- `bindCustomerLogin(id, principal)` — bind a login principal to a customer\n  account, clearing any prior binding on that principal. Returns `null` when\n  the customer does not exist.\n- `getMyCustomer()` — resolve the signed-in caller's own customer account\n  (returns `null` when the caller has no linked account).\n\n### Products\n- `listProducts(filter)` — list products. `filter` =\n  `{ search : ?Text; category : ?Text; activeOnly : ?Bool }`.\n- `getProduct(id)` — fetch one product.\n- `createProduct(input)` — create a product. `input` =\n  `{ name; sku; unit; unitPrice; category }`.\n- `updateProduct(id, input)` — edit a product. `input` adds `active`.\n- `deactivateProduct(id)` — set a product inactive without deleting history.\n\n### Invoices\n- `listInvoices(filter)` — list invoices. `filter` =\n  `{ search : ?Text; status : ?InvoiceStatus; customerId : ?CustomerId;\n  fromDate : ?Timestamp; toDate : ?Timestamp }`.\n- `getInvoice(id)` — invoice detail with linked payments and proof ids.\n- `createInvoice(input)` — create an invoice. `input` =\n  `{ customerId; lines : [{ productId; quantity }]; issuedAt; dueAt; notes }`.\n  Line totals and the grand total are computed from current product prices.\n\n### Payments and proofs\n- `listPayments(filter)` — list payments. `filter` =\n  `{ search : ?Text; status : ?PaymentStatus; customerId : ?CustomerId }`.\n- `getPayment(id)` — fetch one payment.\n- `recordPayment(input)` — record a manual payment. `input` =\n  `{ invoiceId; amount; paidAt; method; reference }`. Creates an approved\n  payment and a receipt, and recalculates the invoice.\n- `listProofs(filter)` — list transfer proofs. `filter` =\n  `{ status : ?ProofStatus; customerId : ?CustomerId }`.\n- `getProof(id)` — fetch one transfer proof.\n- `approveProof(id)` — approve a pending proof, creating the linked payment and\n  receipt and updating the invoice balance.\n- `rejectProof(id, note)` — reject a pending proof with a review note; the\n  invoice balance is unchanged.\n\n### Debts\n- `listDebts()` — every customer with an outstanding balance, with aging.\n- `getDebtSummary()` — aggregate outstanding balance, customer count, and aging.\n- `getCustomerDebt(customerId)` — one customer's debt detail with invoices.\n\n### Settings\n- `getSettings()` — read the shop profile and bank details. Callable by anyone,\n  including anonymous callers.\n- `updateSettings(input)` — update the shop profile, bank details, and\n  numbering settings. `input` =\n  `{ shopName; address; taxId; phone; bankName; accountName; accountNumber;\n  promptPayRef; invoicePrefix; receiptPrefix; defaultPaymentTermsDays }`.\n\n### Notifications\n- `listManagerNotifications(filter)` — manager notifications, newest first.\n  `filter` = `{ unreadOnly : ?Bool; limit : ?Nat }`.\n- `countUnreadManagerNotifications()` — unread manager notification count.\n- `markManagerNotificationRead(id)` — mark one as read.\n- `markAllManagerNotificationsRead()` — mark all as read; returns the count\n  newly marked.\n\n### Documents\n- `getInvoiceDocument(id)` — printable Thai invoice document.\n- `getReceiptDocument(id)` — printable Thai receipt document.\n- `getDebtNoticeDocument(customerId)` — printable Thai debt notice document.\n\n## Customer endpoints\n\nThese derive the customer from the caller principal and never accept a\nclient-supplied customer id.\n\n- `getMyCustomer()` — the caller's own customer account.\n- `claimCustomerAccount(id)` — bind the caller's own principal to an unclaimed\n  customer account. Returns `null` when the account does not exist or already\n  has a login principal.\n- `listMyInvoices()` — the caller's invoices, newest first.\n- `getMyInvoice(id)` — one of the caller's invoices, or `null` if it is not\n  theirs.\n- `listMyPayments()` — the caller's payments, newest first.\n- `listMyReceipts()` — the caller's receipts, newest first.\n- `getMyReceipt(id)` — one of the caller's receipts, or `null` if it is not\n  theirs.\n- `getMyDebt()` — the caller's debt detail with aging and invoices.\n- `uploadProof(input)` — upload a bank-transfer proof against an invoice.\n  `input` = `{ invoiceId; amount; transferredAt; imageKey; note }`. The proof is\n  created with status `#pending` for manager review.\n- `listMyNotifications(filter)` — the caller's notifications, newest first.\n- `countUnreadMyNotifications()` — the caller's unread notification count.\n- `markMyNotificationRead(id)` — mark one of the caller's notifications read.\n- `markAllMyNotificationsRead()` — mark all of the caller's notifications read;\n  returns the count newly marked.\n\n## Data intelligence (OQL)\n\nThe backend exposes its persisted, queryable data through the Object Query\nLayer. `schema()` returns the discoverable entity schema and `execute(query)`\nruns a JSON query. All entities are **controller-only**: they are readable by\nthe platform's Data Intelligence agent and not by end users. Customer row\nscoping for end users is enforced by the customer endpoints above, not by OQL\nauthorization.\n\nEntities: `customer`, `product`, `invoice`, `payment`, `proof`, `receipt`.\n";
    doc;
  };
};
